    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`, and all four requirements work in a quick test using a stub transport.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Timeouts:** connect is 5 seconds; read, write and pool are 30 seconds. The timeout is set on both the `OpenAI` client and the HTTP client, because `OpenAI` sends its own timeout with every request and would otherwise override the HTTP client's.\n- **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n- **Logging:** a request event hook logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. The hook runs on every send, so retries are logged too.\n- **Transport:** when you pass `transport`, the HTTP client uses it. When it's `None`, the client uses its normal default.\n- The HTTP client is built with `openai.DefaultHttpxClient` rather than a plain `httpx.Client`, so it keeps OpenAI's default connection settings. That includes following redirects.\n\n**Checks:**\n- I used a stub transport that returned 500 twice and then 200. `app.http` logged `GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models` three times (the first try plus two retries), and both clients showed `Timeout(connect=5.0, read=30.0, write=30.0, pool=30.0)`.\n- `pytest -q`: 1 passed. The only existing test checks the logger name, so there are no tests yet for timeouts, retries, logging or the transport.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- Context7 returned \"Monthly quota exceeded\" on both lookups, so I couldn't follow the project rule to check the docs there first. Instead I checked the API against the installed `openai` 2.44.0 and httpx source in `.venv`.\n- The test script `smoke_check.py` is still in the project root because deleting it needed your approval. You can delete it, or I can turn it into a proper test in `tests/` if you'd like the retry and logging behaviour covered.\n\nNo dependencies were added or changed."
